@namespace Raptor21.RCL.Layout
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Sections

@* =================================================================================================
   Where the page's title lands inside the host's PERSISTENT mobile bar.

   The bar itself must live outside the swapped region — it is `position: fixed`, and Safari samples
   the status-bar tint from fixed chrome, so a bar re-created on every navigation flashes the tint to
   a flat colour. The title, however, belongs to the page. This element resolves that: the container
   is permanent, only its children change.

   The id belongs to this component, not to the consumer. It is the contract between the server
   section outlet below and `TOPBAR_SLOT` in `runtime/page-chrome.ts`; a consumer hand-writing
   `<div id="rg-topbar-slot">` would be depending on an undocumented string. Placing this component is
   optional — the projector no-ops when it is absent, and `RaptorPageChrome`'s stylesheet guards keep
   the in-page heading visible in that case, so a layout without a mobile bar is a supported setup
   rather than a page with no heading at all.
   ================================================================================================= *@

<div id="rg-topbar-slot" class="rg-topbar-slot">
    <SectionOutlet SectionName="@RaptorPageChrome.TopbarSectionName"/>
</div>
